  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)({x}^{2}+x-6)}{{x}^{2}(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}({x}^{2}+x-6)}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2$ and $x=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/31f16682ad863f5f320130705ac57415a74340f3fe73a67a03b4df258c2577e7.png)",
